{
    "_comment": "Lands that get a rendered map. rect: cells x0 y0 x1 y1 of the sheet, or auto (the land above water, the markers and a margin). host: the level 32 LOD chunk the sheet's mesh is named after, or auto (the chunk under the middle of the sheet). onamz: the map offset height. usable: the map data's usable size. Other lands keep their paper map or their 3D map. winter: false for lands the permanent winter does not reach, which then keep their own colours. surround: true blends the land beyond the markers into smooth snow and rock, fading its object LOD. soften: 0 to 1 for lands whose mountain LOD is coarser than Skyrim's, measured in PLAN.md. road_extra: more landscape textures to draw as paths, for a land whose paths are painted in plain dirt. sea: true for a land with an open sea. direct: terrain and buildings from the land's records, not LOD. ambient, tone: the day light. placed: also draw the structures the land's references place, from their full models. single: day or night: one picture, for a land with no sky cycle. lights: true marks every light and glowing plant the references place. water: shallow and deep colours, day then night. water_style 1: Apocrypha. placed all: rock as well. land_soft: shade terrain from the map's heights, and lay snow on gentle dark ground. hide: cell rectangles of filler terrain to leave out. placed all: every structure and rock from its full model, instead of object LOD. ceiling: for a cave land, leave out what stands this far above the floor. true_coast: false takes the coast from the LOD's heights instead of the land's records. terrain_lines: true also traces the terrain's edges, as the approved Skyrim map was drawn. keep: the owner approved this land's picture; a rerun leaves it unless the land is named with --world. ppc: this land's sheet size in pixels a cell. tile_ppc: tiles over the sheet at this size. alt_textures: read the texture swaps on model records. road_meshes: road models drawn as flat stone in road_colour. road_paint: painted roads take this colour rather than their texture's. all_water: the sea covers all its ground. relief: strength of the ground's shading. flatten: x0 y0 x1 y1 z, filler cells levelled. edge_cells: width of the sheet's soft edge. void_below: terrain at this height is the land's unused flat ground, and melts into the surround. retouch: keep = outlines in cells, everything outside them, or inside its remove outlines, becomes smooth ground; cosmetic, for what the player cannot reach. land_colour: the LOD ground drawn in this colour, keeping its pattern, for a cave whose LOD ground is bare dirt. retouch heal: rectangles whose drawn outline is taken out. sweep_note: why a land may stage with right angles outside buildings (tools/right_angles.py). road_soft: passes of softening over the painted roads, taking out their stair steps. facet_soft: 0 to 1, how far model triangles lean to straight up, which hides low-detail facets.",
